abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution.
  Version v23.2 keeps everything in v23.1: CORE.md opens with what a
  functional world model is and follows one model of learning, read as a
  network, in eight steps, and formalization/ebe-core/EbECore.lean audits 96
  machine-checked results. It adds, outside the core, a working note on what
  one turn of learning consists of, with three core-Lean modules. In a model
  of learning as ruling out possibilities, in a world that stands still, it
  states a set of operations and conditions that are jointly sufficient for a
  learning turn; shows that an error which none of a learner's own operations
  tells from the truth survives its own honest turns, and can be removed by
  another learner with a different operation; separates being told a result
  from being taught an operation; and puts the same loop on a resource ledger.
  The work went through two outside reviews, the assistant's own adversarial
  review and an independent literature audit, all kept in the repository with
  the responses. The audit's judgment is accepted: the work is mainly a small
  formal reconstruction of known ideas (candidate elimination, observational
  indistinguishability, learning about methods, elementary resource
  accounting) and is not presented as new theory; no claim was judged a
  sharpening, and two counterexamples to its interpretation were accepted and
  corrected. The Discovarian creed gains two sections in draft, on what a
  learner does and what has to hold. A concept note proposes, as a proposal
  and not as law, a protected interest in a person's routes of correction
  under the safeguard that fallible is not incompetent; no lawyer has read it.
  Retained from v23.1: cooperative error identification, acting under time,
  models for acting in a changing world, and a working space on the Yang–Mills
  mass gap that is handed over to others and contains no mass-gap result. No
  human expert has reviewed the additions of this release. DIALOGUE.md records
  how the author and an AI assistant build the model together, now in 49
  entries. The release title uses ‘simulation of reality’ to mean the internal
  model through which a system experiences and acts in the world, not a claim
  that reality itself is simulated. Formal verification establishes
  implications under explicit premises; empirical, causal, political and
  normative interpretations remain open. The original repository material is
  dual-licensed under CC BY 4.0 OR Apache-2.0 as documented in
  DUAL-LICENSING.md; CC BY 4.0 is supplied here as the single Zenodo archival
  metadata value because the GitHub-Zenodo metadata path accepts one license
  value.
